From 136dd32c01ead3ce429aaa4bc5782f6a4891d8ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Tung <kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 20:23:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fw_update: stop sensor polling during update when configured

This commit introduces the StopSensorPolling condition for firmware
updates, following the concept defined in the code-update design [1].

Some devices cannot tolerate PLDM sensor/event traffic during firmware
updates. Add a per-component 'StopSensorPolling' setting to the
condition config, alongside the existing PreUpdateTarget and
PostUpdateTarget settings.

When enabled, pause sensor polling for the device's terminus before the
update starts and resume it after the update completes, regardless of
the outcome.

[1] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/docs/+/93751

Tested on YV5:
```
root@bmc:~# journalctl -u pldmd | grep -iE "stop|resume|firmware|Component"
Aug 25 06:36:21 bmc pldmd[748]: Firmware update condition for component CXL_Component_0 sets sensor polling stop to True
Aug 25 06:36:21 bmc pldmd[748]: Firmware update condition for component NIC_Component_1 sets sensor polling stop to True
Aug 25 06:38:22 bmc pldmd[748]: Paused sensor polling for TID 2 during firmware update
Aug 25 06:38:22 bmc pldmd[748]: Component at endpoint ID '10' with version '26.07.00' can be updated
Aug 25 06:51:10 bmc pldmd[748]: Component endpoint ID '10' and version '26.07.00' transfer complete.
Aug 25 06:51:11 bmc pldmd[748]: Component endpoint ID '10' and version '26.07.00' verification complete.
Aug 25 06:52:56 bmc pldmd[748]: Component endpoint ID '10' with '26.07.00' apply complete.
Aug 25 06:52:56 bmc pldmd[748]: Resumed sensor polling for TID 2 after firmware update
Aug 25 06:52:56 bmc pldmd[748]: Firmware update time: 873545.005563ms
```

Gerrit link: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/pldm/+/93664

Change-Id: I6e45faaa6545534000cf77e6b8d30df37ff243a5
Signed-off-by: Kevin Tung <kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com>
